y to  present  and so this comes with a lot of program  resources that we've developed that we  think could be very helpful for all of  you  now we tried to combine all of these  resources on our onyx logic training  portal that has a variety of different  types of asynchronous courses as well as  more guided programs that are led by  experts in bioinformatics and we provide  for  all of the participants of this program  access to specific  sessions that you can access to  understand whether that program is right  for you  and this is typically done in  collaboration with other universities  and organizations  so not only do you get the opportunity  to learn about the topic but also  interact from particip with participants  from these different institutions  but you can find all of this on our  omixlogic portal which is  [Music]  learn.omixlogic.com you will find there  adapted courses for you personally based  on your experience  as you progress that will change you  will be able to track your progress  and see how you've improved your  understanding of the basic topics  as well as the application of these  different tools  in different types of challenges and  projects like this  is an example of a project on the origin  and pathogenesis  of the novel coronavirus and we have  many other examples like that as well  so behind this what we also provide is  access to user-friendly big data  analysis tools and this is a critical  component of this program  you get access to five terabytes of  storage which allows you to process and  analyze large data sets that allow you  to use  advanced statistical methods and machine  learning  as well as multi-omics integration and  several tools that will be helpful for  biological interpretation now this  infrastructure is limited we do not give  everybody  access to that same resource and the  research fellows that have joined this  program  have that kind of a special level of  access where you can actually  conduct a full res