that can help  answer your specific questions you have  to let us know so remember that it's  your responsibility to reach out to us  and let us know what is it that you're  interested in doing  and how we can best help you finally  when you get to this process  of preparing your analysis results  you are going to be also following  examples of many others that have gone  through the same process  and so that's where your peer community  is going to be very helpful  so when you present and you go through  these iterations  of drafts you will see that we can help  you the most by  making that presentation better and  helping you  present something to external evaluators  at poster presentations if you're  looking to submit a research article  in a much more prepared way and so the  outcomes  of this process are very important to  keep in mind right so have a goal when  you're joining this program have a  specific goal  you will have a guarantee and a positive  outcome if you properly identify  what that outcome for you is maybe you  just want to understand  the specific challenges and data sets  and gain training  that's one option maybe you want to  develop some skills like processing data  and analyzing data maybe you want to  join  an independent project or a group  project so that's another option you  don't have to work on this on your own  we will hear today from root v who has  completed an independent project and  hopefully she will continue to work on  a group project next so some people will  actually announce  that i'm working on this topic and i'm  looking for collaborators  that's why it's important to be a part  of the slack channel in our community  so that everybody can get to know each  other not only hear their presentations  in the final results  so let me briefly tell you what are some  of the recent examples  of people that have successfully  completed the research  projects and the research fellowship  april zhang just recently completed a  research fellowship  she's a high school student and now she  got accepted to  berkeley for bioinformatics  undergraduate  and we have a recording of her  presentation that you can take a look at  i'm gonna post  uh the link right here  see mine dolaner she will be presenting  in the next uh core in the next  psionics session that will happen  uh i believe tomorrow but i will let uh  rudy talk about that in a little bit  uh supantha who is from bangladesh  and he is uh also you can see his  project presentation he will also be  presenting at the cyanux club  uh dr anita ganza uh who is right now  working still on a number of research  projects together with  uh her team and we have collaborated  with her and her  team to recently present her project  at the louisiana biomedical research  network  so please take a look at some of these  links and you'll kind of see  how this works for some of the other  people that you might  be following in their footsteps and all  of them  are of course going to be available as  somebody that can give you  hints and tips and maybe some guidance  on  how to complete a project and make it  impactful  so that's an important part of the  outcome as well when you think of  completing this project think about how  are you going to use it to also advance  your personal career and learning  and so we have an example of urja that  finished her  uh project a while back andres  who has completed his project and will  be presenting next week  we have others that are uh selected to  be a  part of this program and so please do  share that information with others  with your network to help them  understand what you are working on  so now let me pass this on to  uh dr harpreed or sonalika i don't know  who is going to announce  who is going to be presenting next so  that you can kind of see  where this process will lead you as you  join this research fellowship
 

